<ol class="space-y-3">
  <!-- The run this table belongs to, so each row links to that target's results
       for this date rather than to its current page.
       Builds render inside their parent's row, the same as on the board. Without
       this guard a run page listed a build both nested under its project and
       again as a peer beside it, so the two surfaces disagreed about whether a
       build competes with the engine it is a build of. -->
  <!-- Same reading as the board: the row that stands for its project, which is
       not always the reference build. When that build has no result the
       grouping promotes another to stand for it, and filtering on the slug
       alone dropped the project from this run entirely. The slug stays as the
       reading for a run restored from the committed fallback, which predates
       the flag. -->
  <standings-row webc:for="row of run.standings" webc:if="standsForProject(row)" :row="row" :run-id="run.id"></standings-row>
</ol>
